  "worked_solution": "We have $k(x)=3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to ${k}^{\u2032}(0).$ From step 6, the derivative is\n\n$$\n{k}^{\u2032}(x)=3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{\u2032}(0) & =3{e}^{0}-3(0)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =3-0-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
